{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"exact-identities-and-reductions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/exact-identities-and-reductions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","span":{"end_byte":190836,"end_line":2055,"start_byte":157177,"start_line":1656},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity"],"id":"long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.52 (Uniqueness of an integer recurrence with a vanishing scaled limit)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.52, p. 59, label thm:tempered-orbit-rigidity","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For any nonnegative-integer coefficient sequence $c:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N$ with $c(n)\\le\nn$: the binary coefficient series $X_c = \\sum'_{n\\ge 1} c(n)/2^n$ is rational iff there exists a positive integer multiplier $v$ and an integer orbit $u:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb Z$ satisfying the exact carry recurrence $u(N{+}1)=2u(N)-v\\cdot c(N{+}1)$ together with the condition $u(N)/2^N\\to0$. Every integer sequence satisfying both conditions obeys $u(N) = v\\cdot T_c(N)$ exactly, where $T_c(N)=\\sum_{j\\ge 1} c(N{+}j)/2^j$ is the scaled tail. For each fixed $v$ there is at most one such sequence. Positivity of the orbit alone is deliberately *not* used as an equivalent criterion: a homogeneous $2^N$-scaled perturbation can be added to any orbit without breaking the recurrence, so the limit condition cannot be dropped. The choices $c=c_A$ for Problem 257 and $c=\\varphi$ for Problem 249 both satisfy $0\\le c(n)\\le n$. The telescoping argument is given again, with an example, in Theorem 6.105.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-tempered-orbit-rigidity%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.binaryCoeffSeries_rationa